==English==
===Noun===
'''bowman'''  (plural ''[[bowmen]]'')
# an [[archer]]
# the person, in a [[team]] or [[oarsmen]], nearest the [[bow]]

Archers when placed in an army (for the meaning of an archer wielding a bow and a quiver of arrows) they are placed near the nd with knights or spearmen in the front to give them cover so they can take out soldiers from afar. They are mainly skilled with a bow but may wield a short sword or a dagger of somesort to fight upclose.

